caption: Instancing
engine-rule: instancing

Word is Non-Instanced by default. A shared language, lexicon, grammar, rune set, or symbolic system used by every practitioner remains Non-Instanced even when practitioners learn different Words, skills, phrases, or techniques.

A Word Tradition is Institutionally Instanced only when a school, order, lineage, language tradition, or other institution owns a fixed access-defining lexicon, grammar, correspondence set, or expression catalogue that is transmitted as a package. It is Personally Instanced only when each practitioner receives or constructs an individual access-defining vocabulary, grammar, correspondence set, or syntax. Learning different subsets of a shared language does not by itself create an instance.
